title: Württemberg Affairs
new-page: true
is-card: true
view-if: in_wurttemburg_spd == 1 and wurttemberg_affairs_timer <= 0
on-arrival: wurttemberg_affairs_timer += 6; month_actions += 1
tags: landtag_affairs
card-image: img/braun.jpg
#subtitle: The state government of Württemberg presents an opportunity...

= Württemberg Affairs

Württemberg has historically been a more difficult state for our party, with a particularly strong independent agrarian party. We intend to change that.

We can enact policies in Württemberg.

- @build_ties: We can use push our state party to strengthen ties with the other local parties.
- @pursue_policy: We can push our state party to pursue policy goals on the local level.
- @paramilitary: We can pursue policies regarding the local paramilitaries.
- @root: No new policies are needed.
- @easy_discard

@build_ties

- @build_ties_uspd: Push our state party to strenghten ties with the state USPD.

@pursue_policy

- @bureaucracy: Purge the bureaucracy of reactionary elements.
- @land_reform: We can conduct land reform on a local level.
- @agricultural_finance: We can provide agricultural financing on the state level.
- @pro_consumer: We can negotiate for lower prices with local farmers.

@paramilitary

- @persecute_sa: Use our state offices to target and prosecute the state SA.
- @persecute_rfb: Use our state offices to target and prosecute the state RFB.
- @persecute_sh: Use our state offices to target and prosecute the state Stalhelm.
- @recruit_rsb: Use our state offices to promote recruitment for the Reichsbanner.

@land_reform
unavailable-subtitle: [? if judicial_reform < 2 : The judiciary would never allow this. ?]
choose-if: judicial_reform >= 2
on-arrival: land_reform += 1; rural_spd += 5*(1-dissent); rural_nsdap -= 4*(1-dissent); unemployed -= 1 if unemployed >= 5; dvp_relation -= 5; z_relation -= 4; left_strength += 8; left_dissent -= 5; rural_sol += 3; rural_policy += 1; coup_progress += 1; agriculture_goal_completed += 1; socialism += 1

With our policy of land reform, we are acquiring farmland from large estates, and giving the land to farmworkers' associations and small peasants. In essence, this brings class struggle to the countryside, breaking the semi-feudal property relations present in East Prussia and other areas with large estates. The bourgeois parties and large farmers despise our intrusion into the sacredness of private property, while leftists are cautiously optimistic.

@agricultural_finance
on-arrival: agricultural_finance += 1; rural_spd += 5*(1-dissent); rural_nsdap -= 3*(1-dissent); peoples_party_support += 1; center_dissent += 5; left_dissent += 4; rural_sol += 4; rural_policy += 1; economic_growth += 0.2;

We have increased financial support for small farmers, providing access to credit and insurance, saving them from privation. The left and center of our party are opposed to our rural policy, seeing these policies as giveaways to petit-bourgeois farmers.

@pro_consumer
on-arrival: budget -= 1; pro_consumer += 1; workers_spd += 4*(1-dissent); unemployed_spd += 4*(1-dissent); workers_sol += 4; coalition_dissent += 1 if black_thursday_seen; economic_growth += 0.2

We have increased state purchasing of food staples to provide to urban workers and the poor. This benefits workers more than it benefits farmers, as we are negotiating for lower purchase prices. [? if black_thursday_seen and (in_weimar_coalition or in_grand_coalition) : Our coalition partners consider this policy to be a wasteful handout. ?]

@bureaucracy
on-arrival: wurttemberg_nsdap -= 0.02 if wurttemberg_nsdap >= 0.6; wurttemberg_nsdap -= 0.02 if year < 1930 and wurttemberg_nsdap >= 0.6; wurttemberg_dnvp += 0.02 if year < 1930 and wurttemberg_dnvp < 1.2; wurttemberg_dnvp -= 0.03 if year >= 1930 and wurttemberg_dnvp >= 0.8; wurttemberg_other += 0.02 if year >= 1930 and wurttemberg_other < 1.2; wurttemberg_dvp += 0.01 if year >= 1930; nationalism -= 5; pacifism += 1; democratization += 1; pro_republic += 3*(1-dissent); new_middle_spd += 2*(1-dissent) if democratization >= 3; new_middle_spd += 2*(1-dissent) if democratization >= 4; coup_progress += 0.5

The bureaucracy is deeply reactionary, and many abuse their power to favor the political right. By removing the pro-monarchy and pro-dictatorship elements, we can democratize it. Some of our opponents claim that we are infringing on individual freedoms, but perhaps the security of the republic requires it.

@persecute_sa 
on-arrival: sa_strength -= 500; uspd_relation += 3

As it turns out, the Nazi SA has many allies in the police and bureaucracy, undermining our efforts. Nevertheless, the SA is substantially weakened by our efforts.

@persecute_sh 
on-arrival: sa_strength -= 250; dvp_relation -= 5; uspd_relation += 3

Unsurprisingly, the Stalhelm has many allies in the police and bureaucracy, undermining our efforts. Nevertheless, our efforts bear some fruit.

@persecute_rfb 
on-arrival: rfb_strength -= 1000; uspd_relation -= 10; z_relation += 3; dvp_relation += 3

The reactionary elements in the police and bureaucracy enthusiastically carry out these orders – rather more enthusiastically than we’d like, in fact. Nevertheless, our efforts bear clear fruit.

@recruit_rsb
On-arrival: rb_strength += 250; rb_militancy += 0.05; z_relation -= 2; dvp_relation -= 3

We have used our state offices to promote recruitment to the Reichsbanner. The other state parties decry this as an abuse of office, but we ignore their protests.
